## Node
node_modules/

## Generated into the project's wwwroot by the client build (Client/). The hand written
## BackOffice/Common/**/*.html beside them IS source and is tracked.
##
## Because these are generated and ignored, a build that has not run the client build produces a
## package that installs cleanly and then does nothing. The csproj fails the pack in that case
## rather than shipping one - see the VerifySignatureFieldAssets target.
src/Integrious.Umbraco.Forms.SignatureField/wwwroot/App_Plugins/UmbracoFormsSignatureField/BackOffice/Css/
src/Integrious.Umbraco.Forms.SignatureField/wwwroot/App_Plugins/UmbracoFormsSignatureField/BackOffice/signature-field.js*
src/Integrious.Umbraco.Forms.SignatureField/wwwroot/App_Plugins/UmbracoFormsSignatureField/BackOffice/signature-property-editor-ui.element.js*
src/Integrious.Umbraco.Forms.SignatureField/wwwroot/App_Plugins/UmbracoFormsSignatureField/FrontEnd/
